# Build context for infra/Dockerfile is the repository root.
#
# The entries that matter are not about size. `.env` would bake whatever API
# key is on the building machine into every layer of the image. `.tools/` would
# ship a Windows tectonic.exe into a Linux container, where it cannot run but
# would still satisfy the installer's "already installed" check. And `.venv/`
# would copy compiled wheels for the wrong platform.

**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

backend/.tools/
backend/.tectonic-cache/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

**/*.db
**/storage/
**/*.pdf
**/*.aux
**/*.log

# The API image does not serve the frontend; Vercel builds that separately.
frontend/
docs/
